  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">C227C, Civic Tech Niger</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">the NGO Citoyens 227 Connect&#xe9;s decides to implement the specific project Civic Tech 227 which will allow young people and women to be equipped on local citizenship issues, to have access to information, to evaluate local public action and to celebrate the model citizen of our community. Niger&apos;s democratic context is marked by a lack of transparency in the management of public affairs, a lack of access to information by citizens on public services, a disconnection of citizens from civic, public and political life, and a lack of interest among young people and women to the detriment of an old political class.
This is what leads today in our society to bad practices such as racketeering, corruption, charity of life, frustration, violence and violent extremism.
To counter this, it is imperative that the citizen be placed back at the heart of the decision-making process. Open government issues are opportunities forNiger to opportunities for Niger to engage in open government policy to promote to promote transparency, fight against corruption, and boost the economy. corruption, boost civic engagement, and take advantage of new civic new civic technologies.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org ref="XM-DAC-7" role="1" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ministry of Foreign Affairs NL</narrative>
  </participating-org>
  <participating-org role="4" type="90">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In October 2020, more than 5,000 young people from 22 countries in the Maghreb and sub-Saharan Africa took the Citizen Connections online course for six (6) weeks dedicated to the challenges and opportunities of Civic Tech in Africa. 800 obtained the certification. 500 young citizens from Francophone Africa responded to the call for applicationslaunched in November 2020 for the selection of 25 laureates with innovative and innovative and committed projects.The Civic Tech 227 Project, led by a young Nigerian, was one of the 25 selected out of 500 having benefited from an incubation during eight (8) months which emerged the creation of a young organization called &quot;Citoyens 227 Connected&quot; equipped by African and European experts and mentors on strategic aspects and accompanied by thelocal incubator on operationaloperational aspects in the realization of its project by coordinating various expertises and connections, in order to promote the deployment of its Civic Tech 227 innovation to support innovative civic participation in Niger.The NGO Citizens 227 Connected is conceived as an entrepreneurial project for the development of citizen and digital initiatives for better governance, a stronger participation of citizens in the decisions that are made and also in the resolution of issues that concern them directly.For more information, please discover the interview of the promoter of the Civic Tech 227 project and Executive Coordinator of the Citizens 227 Connected Organization: https://fb.watch/aQTygqzsxK/</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ONG Citoyens 227 Connect&#xe9;s</narrative>
  </participating-org>
